   "id": "zevachim.102b.6",
   "daf": "102b",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "אֲפִילּוּ טָמֵא בִּשְׁעַת זְרִיקַת דָּמִים, וְטָהוֹר בִּשְׁעַת הֶקְטֵר חֲלָבִים – אֵינוֹ חוֹלֵק. הָא טָהוֹר בִּשְׁעַת זְרִיקַת דָּמִים, וְטָמֵא בִּשְׁעַת הֶקְטֵר חֲלָבִים – חוֹלֵק;",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «Even» if the priest was «ritually impure» only «at the time of the sprinkling of the blood» of the offering, «and» he was «pure at the time of the burning of the fats,» he still «does not receive a share» of the meat. The Gemara notes: «Consequently,» one can infer that a priest who was «pure at the time of the sprinkling of the blood,» even one who was «impure at the time of the burning of the fats, does receive a share.»"
  }
 ],
